  "id": "DrugBank_DB00494 - MONDO_10482",
  "verbalization": "Entacapone, through its indications, appears to be linked to X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome via a chain of drug–disease relationships. The evidence suggests that Entacapone is associated with Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism and Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease, both of which are indicated to treat X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome. This implies that Entacapone may exert a therapeutic effect on this condition, possibly through mechanisms that involve modulating dopaminergic pathways or other neurochemical processes. The presence of multiple pathways linking Entacapone to the syndrome suggests a potential role in disease management, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these indications highlights the possibility that Entacapone could be a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of X-linked Parkinsonism-spasticity Syndrome, though further research is needed to confirm its efficacy and mechanism of action.",
